"Wind weather title / alert" = "Wind classification";
"Wind weather message / alert" = "Calm: < 0.3 m/s\nQuiet: 0.3—1.5 m/s\nLight: 1.6—3.3 m/s\nModerate: 3.4—5.4 m/s\nFresh: 5.5—7.9 m/s\nStrong: 8.0—10.7 m/s\nNear Gale: 10.8—13.8 m/s\nGale: 13.9—17.1 m/s\nStrong Gale: 17.2—20.7 m/s\nStorm: 20.8—24.4 m/s\nViolent Storm: 24.5—28.4 m/s\nHurricane: >32.7 m/s";

"Temperature weather title / alert" = "Feels like";
"Temperature weather message / alert" = "The indicator «Feels like» may differ from the actual temperature, reflecting how the temperature is perceived by a person. The «Feels like» indicator is influenced by wind characteristics and humidity levels.";

"Cloud cover weather title / alert" = "Cloud cover";
"Cloud cover weather message / alert" = "Cloud cover is measured as a percentage. It is usually expressed in the parts of the sky occupied by clouds.";

"Humidity weather title / alert" = "Humidity";
"Humidity weather message / alert" = "Relative humidity, or simply humidity, is the ratio of the amount of moisture in the air to the maximum amount that can be contained in the air.";

"Dew point weather title / alert" = "Dew point";
"Dew point weather message / alert" = "The dew point is the value to which the temperature must drop in order for dew to form. This is a convenient way to determine the humidity of the air: the higher the dew point, the more humid the air feels. The dew point coinciding with the current temperature means that the relative humidity of the air is 100% and dew or fog may form.";

"Visibility weather title / alert" = "Visibility";
"Visibility weather message / alert" = "Visibility shows at what distance from yourself you can clearly see objects such as buildings and hills. Visibility is a measure of air transparency and does not take into account the amount of sunlight or the presence of obstacles.";

"Precipitation weather title / alert" = "Precipitation";
"Precipitation weather message / alert" = "The amount of precipitation is the height of the water layer in millimeters that would form on the earth's surface if it were completely flat. The amount of precipitation in millimeters is numerically equal to the mass of water that fell on a horizontal surface of 1 square meter.";

"Pressure weather title / alert" = "Pressure";
"Pressure weather message / alert" = "The table shows deviations from the pressure norm relative to your location. The usual pressure for people is 760 millimeters of mercury. But the normal atmospheric pressure for each person depends on the region in which he is located, and the pressure of the region depends on the altitude of the area.";

"UvIndex weather title / alert" = "UvIndex";
"UvIndex weather message / alert" = "The UV index (UFI), developed by the World Health Organization, indicates the power of ultraviolet radiation. The higher the UV index, the more dangerous it is to be in the sun and the faster it can harm your health. By tracking the UV index, you can decide when to protect yourself from the sun and when it is better not to go outside.";

